---
/** The migration strip (Home 8), with the honest part said rather than buried. */
import Container from "@/components/site/Container.astro";
import Section from "@/components/site/Section.astro";
import SectionHeading from "@/components/site/SectionHeading.astro";
import Button from "@/components/ui/Button.astro";
import Icon from "@/components/ui/Icon.astro";
---

<Section tone="surface" labelledBy="switching-heading">
  <Container>
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <SectionHeading
          id="switching-heading"
          title="Leaving Rewardful, FirstPromoter or LeadDyno? Or a spreadsheet?"
        />
        <p class="mt-6 text-body text-ink-secondary">
          Upload the export as you downloaded it, or any spreadsheet with a header row, or read a
          programme straight from Rewardful or FirstPromoter with your key. Refficks reads it back
          before anything is imported: how many rows, how many it can take, and which lines it
          cannot and why. Nothing happens until you say so. One bad row never loses the file, and
          re-importing never duplicates anyone.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6">
          <Button href="/migrate/" variant="secondary" size="md">
            How migration works
            <Icon name="arrow-right" class="size-4" />
          </Button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-4 lg:col-span-7 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-canvas p-6">
          <h3 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-ink">The honest part.</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-body-sm text-ink-secondary">
            Paid history comes across labelled as the old platform&rsquo;s figure, and never becomes
            payable here. What is still owed can come across as an opening balance, pending until
            you approve it. A ledger that only holds money it can explain is the product.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-canvas p-6">
          <h3 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-ink">Then the shadow run.</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-body-sm text-ink-secondary">
            While the old platform keeps paying, Refficks records what it would have paid, pays
            none of it, and every morning compares the last 28 days partner by partner. At cutover,
            exactly one system pays, and Refficks warns if a partner&rsquo;s earnings drop.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Section>
